  "description": "The Ace is a \"real-deal\" mountain bike for kids from about 8 to 11. It uses a time-tested frame, burly enough for singletrack riding and for taking wee hits and drops. The hydraulic brakes offer control, so kids can learn to confidently feather the brakes as needed, and the brakes can be adjusted so they're right for your kid's reach and hand size. Wide bars, knobby tires, tuneable suspension and a 1x8 drivetrain make it a fully capable bike that's up for north-shore-style trails and full-on downhill ripping.\n\nLightweight aluminum frame is durable and ready to hit the trails\n\nAggressive 24 x 2.0in. tires ready for hardpack, soft surfaces and muddy trails\n\nTektro Jr. hydraulic disc brakes with adjustable reach to match your child's hands\n\nRST Capa T24 suspension fork has 50mm of travel and can be locked-out for ease of climbing\n\n1x8 speed drivetrain features Shimano trigger shifters and 12-32T cassette\n\n32T narrow-wide chainring makes dropping your chain a thing of the past\n\n620mm wide bars for control on bumpy trails\n\nPreload feature on the fork adjusts for different rider weights\n\nLock-on grips prevents unwanted grip twisting and helps with control\n\nFlat pedals provide good grip\n\nBuilt with Shimano® components\n\nSized for kids from 8 to 11 years, or about 135 to 150cm (4ft. 5in. to 4ft. 11in.)\n\nBikes are covered by MEC's Rocksolid Guarantee and Bike Service Agreement. You can bring your bike to any MEC bike shop for free adjustments and minor maintenance for a year after purchase\n\nMEC bikes were designed in Canada. Everything from the frames to the graphics was developed at the MEC Head Office in Vancouver, BC\n\nDue to challenges with supply chain, components may be substituted for comparable parts at any time. The listed build is how MEC intended your bike to arrive, though the manufacturer may need to make a tweak or two to get you riding sooner",
